-   entry .Error   raised when text is not a valid semantic version
+   entry .Error   sollevato quando il testo non è una versione semantica valida

=   entry .Error   raised when text is not a valid semantic version
-     detail
+     detail

-         Error `↯/s.97.1`: _`version` is not a valid semantic version because …_, with one of four
-         reasons: `BadFormat` (_the string did not match the SemVer 2.0 grammar_, such as
-         `1.2` or `1.2.3.4`), `EmptyIdentifier` (_a prerelease or build identifier was
-         empty_, as in `1.2.3-`), `LeadingZero` (_a numeric identifier had a leading zero_,
-         as in `01.1.1` or `1.2.3-0123`) and `InvalidCharacter` (_an identifier contained a
-         character outside `[0-9A-Za-z-]`_). Raised by `Semver.decodable`; a `v"…"` literal
-         reports the same problems as a compile error instead.
-     entry .Reason   why text is not a semantic version: bad format, an empty identifier, a leading zero or a bad character
+         Errore `↯/s.97.1`: _`version` is not a valid semantic version because …_, con uno di
+         quattro motivi: `BadFormat` (_the string did not match the SemVer 2.0 grammar_, come
+         `1.2` o `1.2.3.4`), `EmptyIdentifier` (_a prerelease or build identifier was empty_,
+         come in `1.2.3-`), `LeadingZero` (_a numeric identifier had a leading zero_, come in
+         `01.1.1` o `1.2.3-0123`) e `InvalidCharacter` (_an identifier contained a character
+         outside `[0-9A-Za-z-]`_). Sollevato da `Semver.decodable`; un letterale `v"…"` segnala
+         invece gli stessi problemi come errore di compilazione.
+     entry .Reason   perché il testo non è una versione semantica: formato errato, un identificatore vuoto, uno zero iniziale o un carattere non valido

-       detail
+       detail

